    "title": "Ravi and His Camera",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "My name is Ravi and I love photography. I started two years ago when my uncle gave me an old camera for my birthday. It was a small black camera, and it was not very good, but I took photos every day."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "I take photos of many things: people, buildings, trees and animals. My favourite subject is street life. On Saturday mornings, I go to the market in my town and take photos of the shops and the people. I always ask first if I can take a photo of a person."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Last year I bought a new camera. It was expensive, so I worked in my uncle's shop for three months to pay for it. Now I can take better photos, even at night. I put my best photos on a website, and my friends send me messages about them."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "I want to be a photographer one day. Next month I am joining a photography club at my school. The club meets on Wednesdays at four o'clock. We go outside and take photos, and then we talk about them. I am very excited about it."
      }
    ]
  },
